<content>
  <section><para>In this unit, students will:</para>
<list>
  <item>Decide whether relations define a function and evaluate functions expressed in function notation.</item>
  <item>Graph linear functions on the coordinate plane and identify key features, identify transformations of the parent function \(f(x)=x\), and represent domain and range using inequalities for real-world situations.</item>
  <item>Identify terms of arithmetic and geometric sequences and write a formula for the nth term of arithmetic and geometric sequences, given the value of several of their terms.</item>
</list>
<para>To accomplish these unit-level learning goals, students will complete the following lessons and activities.</para>
<title>Student Readiness for Unit 4</title>
<para>To be ready for this unit, students will need to be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Find the slope of the line that goes through two points on a graph.</item>
  <item>Interpret the meaning of a situation from a graph.</item>
  <item>Use a pattern to find the next term in a sequence.</item>
</list>
<para>This Unit Overview Video will provide a big picture look at the content found in this unit as well as the prerequisite skills that students need for accessing the content in the unit.</para>
<div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-justify-content-center">
  <iframe><iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/mk5ZcsyyzYw;&amp;rel=0" title="YouTube video player"/></iframe>
