<div class="os-raise-accordion">
  <title>Section A: Functions and Their Representations</title>
  <!-- Accordion for Section A Video Overview -->
  <div class="os-raise-accordion-item">
    <button class="os-raise-accordion-header">Overview Video</button>
    <div class="os-raise-accordion-content">
      <div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-justify-content-center">
        <iframe><iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/RlXNDJfsnXs;&amp;rel=0" title="YouTube video player"/></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <!-- Accordion for Section A Standards Alignment Table -->
  <div class="os-raise-accordion-item">
    <button class="os-raise-accordion-header">Texas Essential Knowledge and Skills (TEKS) for Section A</button>
    <div class="os-raise-accordion-content">
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="2"><thead>
          <row>
            <entry>Lesson</entry>
            <entry>Associated TEKS</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>Introduction to Functions</entry>
            <entry>A1.1(A) Define, describe, and identify functions as linear or nonlinear.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Understanding Function Notation</entry>
            <entry>A1.2(B) Interpret statements that use function notation in terms of a context.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Graphing Functions</entry>
            <entry>A1.2(C) Analyze graphs of functions and determine the domain and range, intercepts, zeros, relative maxima and minima, and other characteristics.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Linear Functions and Their Graphs</entry>
            <entry>A1.3(D) Graph functions expressed symbolically and show key features of the graph, by hand in simple cases and using technology for more complicated cases.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Evaluating Functions</entry>
            <entry>A1.4(A) Evaluate functions for specific inputs given the formula of the function.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Application of Functions</entry>
            <entry>A1.5(B) Apply the mathematical process standards to formulate statistical relationships and evaluate their reasonableness based on real-world data.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Unit 4, Section A Quiz</entry>
            <entry>*This quiz assesses the material covered in Section A. Prepare for comprehensive assessments in Unit 4 or the STAAR with additional review and practice.</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </tgroup></table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
